    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Holley saw growth in most divisions despite a slight overall sales dip, signaling resilient demand in its core aftermarket segments. The narrative has shifted from revenue contraction to a return to profitability, with earnings quality now in focus. This challenges prior bearish views and points to stabilization in end markets.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is tightening costs and exiting non-value-added businesses to lift margins. This operational discipline has reversed losses and expanded profitability, earning cautious analyst upgrades and a large institutional vote of confidence. The market is warming to a strategy that prioritizes margin health over top-line scale.",
